backup-manager for Debian and Ubuntu
====================================

Node.js
-------
bkm needs Node.js 22 or later. Ubuntu 26.04 has it. Debian 12 and 13 and
Ubuntu 24.04 ship an older one, so the package cannot be installed there
until a newer "nodejs" package is available, for example from NodeSource
(https://github.com/nodesource/distributions). The project's wiki has the
commands: https://github.com/MateusBMP/backup-manager/wiki/Installation

First run
---------
Nothing is enabled on install and there is no system service. Run "bkm" as
the user who will own the backups: the UI creates the config and installs a
systemd user unit (~/.config/systemd/user/bkm.service) without root.

Database backups need mariadb-dump (package mariadb-client, recommended).

Upgrades and removal
--------------------
A running service keeps the previous code until it is restarted:

    systemctl --user restart bkm

Removing the package keeps every user's config, backups, job history and
unit. To remove the unit, use Uninstall on the Service screen before removing
the package, or afterwards:

    systemctl --user disable --now bkm
    rm ~/.config/systemd/user/bkm.service && systemctl --user daemon-reload
